    "description": "Reshape D5 and D4b around a small curated eval set\n\nUpdates TICKETS.md after the severity policy landed in #32.\n\n- **Preamble** states two facts that shape the eval: a finding a person acted on carries no importance signal in this repo, and the eval is an on-demand tool for one person, not a team gate.\n- **D5** now has a three-pass labeler with a disagreement log in place of the scorer-judge loop, a first curated set of ten small cases from Martian and ReviewBench in TypeScript, JavaScript, Python and Ruby, removal of the four D4a starter cases, a round of policy amendments from the disagreement log, a manual-only eval job in CI, and the rule that the case set never changes during a run. ReviewBench false-positive goldens bring the six-label golden schema into D5.\n- **D4b** grows the set in revisions of about five. Own-repo cases get goldens from a two-family pool. Only dismissed findings come from records, as not-real or don't-post goldens. The `record` source as a positive golden is gone.\n\nNo code change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZgggAoxaZA98nRCMsW",
